    "title": "Driver hits officer, leads police on multi-agency pursuit in Rochester - NewsBreak",
    "text": "ROCHESTER, N.Y. (WROC) — A Waterloo man was taken into custody Wednesday night after allegedly striking a Rochester police officer with a vehicle and leading law enforcement on a multi-agency pursuit, authorities said. According to the Rochester Police Department, officers attempted to stop a suspicious vehicle on North Clinton Avenue when the driver fled the scene, striking an officer in the process. The officer was not injured. A backup officer pursued the suspect in accordance with department policy until the chase was terminated near the interchange of Route 490 and Route 531 by a supervisor. The New York State Police, Monroe County Sheriff’s Office, Ogden Police Department and the NYSP aviation unit continued the pursuit. Authorities eventually apprehended the 26-year-old driver, who faces multiple vehicle and traffic violations along with additional criminal charges, police said. The suspect will also face charges in Rochester. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to RochesterFirst.",
